t—Enforcement of Judgment) (WG-017)\n\nIn a case where the judgment concerns consumer debt, ask the court to stay (pause) a wage garnishment, bank account levy, or other levy because the judgment creditor has not filed Declaration of Address Verification (form WG-015/EJ-135), or because the hearing scheduled by Notice of Hearing on Claim of Exemption (form WG-010/EJ-175) is scheduled to take place more than 30 days after form WG-010/EJ-175 was filed.\n\nGet form WG-017\n\n  * 汉语Get form WG-017 in Chinese Simplified (Chinese Simplified)\n  * 한국어Get form WG-017 in Korean (Korean)\n  * españolGet form WG-017 in Spanish (Spanish)\n\nEffective: July 1, 2026\n\n  * Go to How-to instructions for Debt Collection--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n| California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/find-forms?page=0&query=EM-)\nciteturn1800search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today;   * EJ-137 * Application to Stay Levy or Garnishment (Wage Garnishment—Enforcement of Judgment) Effective: July 1, 2026 汉语 한국어 español\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWG-017/EJ-137 Application to Stay Levy or Garnishment (https://courts.ca.gov/system/files/2025-12/ej137.pdf)\nciteturn1800search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 months ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; APPLICATION TO STAY LEVY OR GARNISHMENT ... July 1, 2026, Mandatory Form\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPUBLISHERS LIST (https://courts.ca.gov/system/files/file/publishers_list_2026-07-01.pdf)\nciteturn1800search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; [Effective on July 1, 2026] ... WG-017/EJ-137* | Rev. | 1 side | Application to Stay Levy or Garnishment (Wage Garnishment—Enforcement of Judgment)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n| California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/fi